                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The principle that the eldest child, traditionally the eldest male, has an exclusive right of inheritance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c2e7752-9579-4a20-bfb3-551d64662126",
                                                "sense_id": "47429696-c7b4-33c3-9b7f-c3fe3f62aed4",
                                                "text": "On these grounds, I contend the mere possession of large property, which is all that primogeniture insures, is by no means a sufficient and unobjectionable qualification for a legislator."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbbacbf0-e3e8-40da-8068-10c38b81a263",
                                                "sense_id": "47429696-c7b4-33c3-9b7f-c3fe3f62aed4",
                                                "text": "Anglo-Saxon kings did not succeed on the basis of primogeniture. All the kings offspring were known as aethelings -- throneworthy -- and from this gene pool the royal family would select the aetheling who seemed best qualified for the job."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f81253c3-5e45-4f9b-b3db-1c7e18b1b429",
                                                "sense_id": "47429696-c7b4-33c3-9b7f-c3fe3f62aed4",
                                                "text": "Primogeniture acting as a law of inheritance in the case of intestacy applied in fact to all real property, however humble. Movables and personal property in this context were subject to equal division, the elder son inheriting all real property as well as his share of the personal property."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0060e95d-15fd-404a-acbc-58f7c8df65aa",
                                                "sense_id": "47429696-c7b4-33c3-9b7f-c3fe3f62aed4",
                                                "text": "He writes as if he is the first privileged male to notice the unfairness of primogeniture (the “hierarchy”, as he likes to call it with sinister emphasis)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d5f274f6-3610-39fe-8839-8d804fc49116",
                                        "entry_id": "97246446-90fe-3b9f-8d6d-8a0c03057d57",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of such a right of inheritance, established by custom or law."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65e4393e-7189-46a4-a092-f010bff3728e",
                                                "sense_id": "d5f274f6-3610-39fe-8839-8d804fc49116",
                                                "text": "The King of Sardinia, by a decree of the 9th of Dec. has abolished—\n1. The prohibition against the erection of primogenitures and feudal rights, enacted by the 9th section of the edict of the 29th of July 1797, or by any other law; restricting, however, to those primogenitures and majorats only which shall be erected in favour of persons[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f183bf8-c3f4-4b6a-be44-1643fa475ca5",
                                                "sense_id": "d5f274f6-3610-39fe-8839-8d804fc49116",
                                                "text": "All primogenitures, trusts, rights of presentation, and every other description of entail on real property, movables, or fixtures, rents, annuities, seigneuries, or of any other kind whatsoever, are suppressed, which are from henceforward restored to the class of absolutely free."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bbf18f5-d2f0-4e31-9937-a4ed2a534fad",
                                                "sense_id": "d5f274f6-3610-39fe-8839-8d804fc49116",
                                                "text": "The American system of land tenures, the abolition of entails and primogenitures, and our methods of transfer of real estate, are all anti-English in their origin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "dd3e6117-f673-40b5-ae5a-650c0bd4249d",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a3e1c0a-4e55-31e8-9282-01558a3a16f3",
                        "source_sense_id": "576da3a3-9c02-3229-997f-4841a8fde277",
                        "target_lang_word": "birthright",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "birthright",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1780ce45-1560-3d4a-bedb-cc1461f99269",
                                        "entry_id": "d6a68246-a8f2-3462-905a-c80c83180180",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something a person is entitled to due to the circumstances of their birth, such as an inheritance or citizenship."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f0632b52-1949-4379-ad2c-b065ca334a32",
                                                "sense_id": "1780ce45-1560-3d4a-bedb-cc1461f99269",
                                                "text": "Not only has suburban life separated the great concentrated masses of our people from their birthright of meadows, fields and woods; of Nature, in her untamed splendour and mystery, most of them have never had so much as a momentary glimpse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec73d87f-507e-4229-bfca-e4d12401e0ab",
                                                "sense_id": "1780ce45-1560-3d4a-bedb-cc1461f99269",
                                                "text": "Though it's the birthright of man to unify and live his life as one / A whisper of the word will let you soar with your soul"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2573ea04-4c7c-40e1-998c-45cbe5b90235",
                                                "sense_id": "1780ce45-1560-3d4a-bedb-cc1461f99269",
                                                "text": "But a practically solo sequence of Dany walking through her old empty house without saying anything for minutes on end is, let’s say, a lot to ask of Emilia Clarke. She’s back at Dragonstone to reclaim her birthright, the seven or so kingdoms."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "13031c05-3e00-4cd4-8b4e-cf0701b45728",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a3e1c0a-4e55-31e8-9282-01558a3a16f3",
                        "source_sense_id": "576da3a3-9c02-3229-997f-4841a8fde277",
                        "target_lang_word": "primogéniture",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "primogéniture",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3bd066ab-5b58-378b-92c9-d69ff6a7e058",
                                        "entry_id": "63cb9d9d-ff61-341e-8666-ca799960e024",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Priorité des droits de succession et d’héritage de l’aîné par rapport aux autres frères et sœurs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Famille"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a37186c6-0361-4f92-8407-18af82aa2f8f",
                                                "sense_id": "3bd066ab-5b58-378b-92c9-d69ff6a7e058",
                                                "text": "La Royauté est indivisible, et déléguée héréditairement à la race régnante de mâle en mâle, par ordre de primogéniture, à l’exclusion perpétuelle des femmes et de leur descendance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e96dd717-1182-4539-accd-0b32bd1d7bdc",
                                                "sense_id": "3bd066ab-5b58-378b-92c9-d69ff6a7e058",
                                                "text": "Le droit à l’héritage, par primogéniture préférablement, parut d’un avantage si manifeste que l’ancien ordre social tendit toujours à généraliser cette institution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84d1738a-2f4c-4dc4-a2d7-56c9079293d0",
                                                "sense_id": "3bd066ab-5b58-378b-92c9-d69ff6a7e058",
                                                "text": "Je me suis étonnée qu’il ait renoncé de gaieté de cœur à Marchienne, en un pays et à une époque où les familles s’arrangeaient pour tourner le Code Napoléon et rester fidèles au principe de la primogéniture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9947d800-6889-4d4f-8b91-a57a92c044fb",
                                                "sense_id": "3bd066ab-5b58-378b-92c9-d69ff6a7e058",
                                                "text": "Dans ce système, il n’y a plus opposition radicale entre descendance et alliance, ni entre descendance par les hommes et descendance par les femmes, car l’objectif premier est la perpétuation de la « maison » et les pratiques de parenté y sont soumises : si la primogéniture et la préférence masculine sont le cas le plus fréquent, il ne s’agit que d’une tendance et diverses mesures de « rattrapage » sont toujours possibles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1580223-29b6-45ae-8cf3-b69179c3e468",
                                                "sense_id": "3bd066ab-5b58-378b-92c9-d69ff6a7e058",
                                                "text": "L’ultimogéniture masculine, selon laquelle le dernier-né des garçons est choisi comme successeur, correspond en général à un type souche faible, moins autoritaire et moins favorable aux garçons que ceux qui pratiquent la primogéniture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
